sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: One chat question through Flowbot
    accDescr: The browser posts the question to the chat API. Flowbot checks the user and token quota, imports the chatbot's server module, and calls start with a handler object and the question. If the module streams, tokens are sent to the browser as Server Sent Events and a final message closes the stream. Token usage is recorded and history is saved.
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser
    participant API as /api/chat (Flowbot)
    participant M as configuration/{id}/server
    participant X as Bot backend (e.g. TTT, LLM)
    participant DB as MongoDB
    B->>API: POST question, chat id, graph ids
    API->>DB: check user and token quota
    API->>M: import, then start(handler, question, onToken)
    M->>X: search, call model
    alt module.streaming is true
        loop each token
            M-->>API: onToken(chunk)
            API-->>B: data: {"type": "token", "chunk": ...}
        end
        API-->>B: data: {"type": "final", "payload": ...}
    else not streaming
        M-->>API: response
        API-->>B: JSON response
    end
    API->>DB: record token usage, save history
